No person or organization may use, copy, run, host, fork, clone, mirror, modify, translate, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell, rent, reverse engineer, extract data from, train or fine-tune a machine learning model on, or create derivative works from any part of this repository, in whole or in part, without prior written authorization from the Owner.

Absence of a reply to a request is not authorization.

## 2. Authorized use

Personnel, contractors, and integrations acting for the Owner (such as Vercel and CI runners) may use this repository only for the purpose, scope, and period stated in their written authorization. Authorization is personal or organization-specific, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, and revocable at any time.

## 3. Brand assets, Marks, and UI Identity (Trade Dress)

The CozyMuseum™ name, logos, wordmarks, backgrounds, imagery, icon sets, and design-source materials are Brand Assets and are treated as strictly protected proprietary property.

While individual colors and open-source fonts remain public or governed by their own licenses (see Section 5), the specific structural combination of these elements—including the compiled Design Tokens, CSS runtime architecture, Liquid Glass UI patterns, and precise palette pairings—constitutes the distinct Trade Dress (Diện mạo thương hiệu) of CozyMuseum.

No person or organization may extract, copy, or reverse-engineer these specific combinations, token structures, or UI patterns to create derivative works, clones, or any product that mimics the CozyMuseum Trade Dress or causes brand confusion, without prior written authorization from the Owner.

## 4. No text or data mining, no model training

The Owner expressly reserves all rights in respect of text and data mining, automated extraction, and the training, fine-tuning, evaluation, embedding, or retrieval-augmented use of any machine learning system on the contents of this repository. This reservation applies to design tokens, CSS rules, JSON manifests, and Brand Assets alike.

